Idiom: a subarray is divisible by `K` when its two bounding prefix sums have the same remainder:

- Sum of subarray `arr[j ... i]` is `sum = prefix[i] - prefix[j - 1]`.
- The sum is divisible by `K` if `sum % K == 0`, or `prefix[i] % k == prefix[j - 1] % k`.
- Conclusion: if two prefix sums have the same remainder, the subarray they bound is divisible by `K`.

Alternatively: two prefix sums with the same remainder differ by a multiple of `K`, and so the subarray they bound has a sum that is a multiple of `K`, i.e. is divisible by `K`.

